{"id": "0f9433b2-504b-4bdd-86c1-66d9ebd58da5", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll scan the customer-managed policies in your account, measure each one's default version, and compare it to the IAM managed-policy size limit. That's a lot of policy documents to read, so I'm running it in the background and will send you a ranked summary when it's done.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_nm6Sw4dYRTg4tGOpiGaCNz", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "iam-policy-size-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Audit all customer-managed IAM policies for size against the IAM managed policy size limit, and rank them by how close they are to the limit.",
  "context": "User wants to know which customer-managed IAM policies are closest to the IAM policy size limit. Use read-only calls only. First confirm the current limit with verify_aws_claim (managed policy limit is believed to be 6,144 characters, and IAM does not count whitespace toward the size). Do not rely on that figure if the docs say otherwise.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1 (agent space home account, IAM is global; use us-east-1)", "Also check any other AWS accounts returned by list_associations that this agent space can assume (monitor/source accounts)"],
  "method_hint": "iam list_policies with Scope=Local (paginate fully, OnlyAttached=false), then for each policy iam get_policy_version on its DefaultVersionId. Compute the size as the character count of the policy document JSON with all whitespace (spaces, tabs, newlines) removed, matching how IAM counts it. Use jmespath filters to keep output small. Do not dump policy documents back; only report computed sizes.",
  "criteria": "Return: total number of customer-managed policies scanned per account; a ranked table of the top ~15 by size (policy name, account, computed size in characters, limit, % of limit, attached count); flag any policies at or above 80% of the limit and any that exceed it; note any policies you could not read. Keep the report concise. Also mention in one line that inline policy limits differ (user 2,048, role 10,240, group 5,120 characters) and that this audit covers only customer-managed policies."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit customer-managed IAM policy sizes against the limit"}], "created_at": null}

